Subject: Adds the init dimension to the register ownership analysis

What this does
  Adds the init dimension to the register ownership analysis.

Why we need it
  The ownership analysis tracked only whether a register held a count, not whether it had ever been written; filling only the registers a function can read before writing needs the second dimension.

What it adds
  `regvm_own_analyze` gains a parallel must-analysis (`REG_INIT_UNINIT`/`REG_INIT_INIT`) seeded from the argument registers, AND-joined at merges, forced UNINIT at exception-handler entries, and advanced by a new `regvm_own_init_step`; the report pass emits the per-function init set (operand reads, non-plain definitions, returns and throws with `own != NONE`), plus `ret_sum`, a function-wide union and `uninit_ret`.

Needs a bytecode version bump
  No.
